window.EB_SB_ADD({"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/animated-armor-bb":{"notes":{"ac":"(13 after construct armor breaks), construct armor"},"flavor":"<p>Objects can be given a semblance of life through the use of rituals or other strange magic, turning them into animated objects. These objects move, work, and fight based on the commands given to them by their creators, who usually set them on guard duty or have them perform menial labor.</p>\n<p>Suits of animated armor might serve as guardians, but sometimes high-end martial academies use them as training partners. They're most often found in wizards' laboratories and ancient dungeons.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Construct Armor","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The animated armor reduces all damage it takes by 9. However, after a critical hit that deals damage, or after its HP drops below 10, its construct armor breaks. Its AC drops to 13 and it no longer reduces damage by 9.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/basilisk-bb":{"flavor":"<p>A basilisk is a reptile that can turn creatures to stone just by looking at them.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Petrifying Glance","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","aura"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature the basilisk can see within 30 feet starts its turn, the basilisk can use its reaction to glance at the creature.</p>\n<p>The creature must attempt a DC 20 Fortitude save. If it fails, it gains the Slowed 1 condition for 1 minute as its body slowly stiffens.</p>"},{"n":"Petrifying Gaze","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The basilisk stares at a creature it can see within 30 feet. If the creature can see the basilisk, that creature must attempt a DC 22 Fortitude save. If it fails and hasn't already gained the slowed condition from Petrifying Glance or this ability, it gains the Slowed 1 condition. If the creature fails this save when it already has the slowed condition from this ability or Petrifying Glance, the creature is permanently turned to stone.</p>\n<p>A creature petrified in this manner that is coated with fresh basilisk blood is instantly restored to flesh. A single basilisk contains enough blood to coat up to 2 creatures in this manner.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/boar-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Foul-tempered and tough, boars are far more dangerous than domesticated pigs. These omnivorous mammals are hunted heavily because their meat is considered a delicacy. Boars are most likely to attack humanoids in self-defense or during their mating season in the winter months, when the males grow an extra inch of tissue to protect their organs as they fight off rivals. In some cultures, boars are trained to become much more aggressive for use as war beasts and guardians. When such boars escape back into the wild, they can become true terrors of the region.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the boar is reduced to 0 Hit Points, it can use its reaction to remain conscious with 1 Hit Point, but it gains the Wounded 1 condition (or increases its wounded value by 1 if it already has that condition). It can't use this ability at wounded 3.</p>"},{"n":"Boar Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The boar Strides twice and then makes a tusk Strike. As long as it moved at least 20 feet, it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to its attack roll.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/brine-shark-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Water elementals roam the endless oceans of the Plane of Water. They can be brought to the world with summoning magic or through natural disasters like floods or hurricanes. Though water elementals can be very destructive, they aren't always malicious. Just as water can bring life to those in need, its waves can pound shores and its rains flood cities. Water elementals are similarly difficult to predict.</p>\n<p>Brine sharks take forms resembling sharks made entirely of water and are fierce, but among the weaker water elementals. They often slip into mortal oceans, competing with natural predators or even joining schools of flesh and blood sharks.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Deep Plunge","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The brine shark dives straight down into the water, swimming up to 100 feet in a straight vertical line. It can use this ability while Grabbing a creature.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the brine shark succeeds at its jaws Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the shark's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/bugbear-prowler-bb":{"gear":["Javelin","Longsword","Leather Armor"],"flavor":"<p>These stealthy and cruel creatures delight in spreading fear and tormenting their victims. Bugbears are the monsters lurking in the closet and hiding under the bed. Preying on remote farmsteads, bugbears reveal their presence with thumps in the night or creaking boards.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Bushwhack","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The bugbear prowler Strides up to 10 feet and attempts to Grapple a creature that can't see them and doesn't know where they are. If the bugbear succeeds, they also deal damage from their fist Strike to that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Mauler","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The bugbear prowler gains a +3 circumstance bonus to damage rolls against creatures they have Grabbed.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/bugbear-tormentor-bb":{"gear":["Dagger","Sickle","Chain Shirt"],"flavor":"<p>The bugbear tormentor seeks to bully their prey as much through psychological intimidation as through physical harm.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The bugbear tormentor's Strikes deal 1d6 extra precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Twin Feint","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The bugbear tormentor makes a dazzling series of attacks with two weapons, using the first attack to throw their foe Off-Guard against a second attack at a different angle. They make one Strike with each of their two melee weapons, both against the same target. The target is automatically off-guard against the second attack. The bugbear tormentor applies their multiple attack penalty to these Strikes normally.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/caligni-dancer-bb":{"gear":["Dagger","Mace"],"flavor":"<p>Caligni lurk in subterranean cities, and they relish the chance to creep above ground at night to steal resources, spy on surface dwellers, or simply cause mischief.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Light Blindness","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When first exposed to bright light, the caligni can't see until the end of their next turn. All squares are difficult terrain for them, and they take a -4 status penalty to Perception. If they try to attack a creature, the attack fails unless they succeed at a DC 11 Flat. Light doesn't blind them again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Final Dance","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a caligni dancer dies, their body dissolves into a swirl of darkness and light. All creatures within 10 feet must succeed at a DC 17 Will save or take a -2 circumstance penalty on all attack rolls for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The caligni dancer deals an additional 1d6 damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/caligni-hunter-bb":{"gear":["Shortsword (2)","Leather Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Caligni lurk in subterranean cities, and they relish the chance to creep above ground at night to steal resources, spy on surface dwellers, or simply cause mischief.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Light Blindness","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When first exposed to bright light, the caligni can't see until the end of their next turn. All squares are difficult terrain for them, and they take a -4 status penalty to Perception. If they try to attack a creature, the attack fails unless they succeed at a DC 11 Flat. Light doesn't blind them again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The caligni hunter deals an extra 1d6 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"},{"n":"Final Fate","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a caligni hunter dies, their body explodes. All creatures within 20 feet must take 5d6 fire. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 19 basic Reflex save.</p>"},{"n":"Darkening Poison","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The next time the hunter deals damage with a shortsword Strike, the target must succeed at a DC 16 Fortitude save or take 1d8 poison damage and treat all creatures as Concealed for 1 round.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/caligni-skulker-bb":{"gear":["Dagger"],"flavor":"<p>Caligni lurk in subterranean cities, and they relish the chance to creep above ground at night to steal resources, spy on surface dwellers, or simply cause mischief.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Light Blindness","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When first exposed to bright light, the caligni can't see until the end of their next turn. All squares are difficult terrain for them, and they take a -4 status penalty to Perception. If they try to attack a creature, the attack fails unless they succeed at a DC 11 Flat. Light doesn't blind them again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Final Night","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a caligni skulker dies, their body dissolves fog of inky darkness. All light sources within 20 feet are extinguished. Any light spells in the area go out for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Darkening Poison","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The next time the skulker deals damage with a dagger Strike, the target must succeed at a DC 16 Fortitude save or take 1d8 poison damage and treat all creatures as Concealed for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The caligni skulker deals an extra 1d6 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/central-spears-bb":{"disable":"<p>A hero must succeed at a DC 18 Thievery check on the triggering floor tiles or the wall sockets in the western wall.</p>","reset":"<p>The central spears reset after 1 minute.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spear Barrage","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature moves into any of the squares in the outlined area, the trap shoots three spears from the western wall. It makes one ranged Strike against the westernmost creature in each row.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/cinder-rat-bb":{"notes":{"per":"smoke vision"},"flavor":"<p>Fire elementals are destructive manifestations of the Plane of Fire. They sometimes come to the world in powerful places of heat and flame where elemental vortexes form, such as in volcanoes.</p>\n<p>Cinder rats are oversized rodents made of smoldering charcoal and elemental fire. Noxious fumes continually bellow from their flaming flesh. Much like terrestrial rats, cinder rats seek out secluded dens and can quickly multiply in number if left unchecked.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Smoke Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The cinder rat ignores the Concealed condition from smoke.</p>"},{"n":"Fetid Fumes","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A cloud of smoke surrounds the cinder rat. All creatures within 5 feet, including the cinder rat, gain the Concealed condition from this smoke. A creature that comes within 5 feet of the cinder rat or begins its turn within 5 feet must succeed at a DC 22 Fortitude save or take a -1 status penalty to all checks and DCs for 1 round <em>(Use Sickened 1)</em>.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/crawling-hand-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Crawling hands form when severed appendages are endowed with a crude sentience by necromantic energies that turn them into tireless killers.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Lifesense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A crawling hand can sense the vital essence of living and undead creatures within 30 feet. This sense can distinguish between the vitality energy animating living creatures and the void energy animating undead creatures, much as sight distinguishes color. However, a crawling hand can't see, so effects that depend on vision or seeing don't work on it.</p>"},{"n":"Throat Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the crawling hand succeeds at its claw Strike against a Medium or smaller creature, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the crawling hand's multiple attack penalty. A creature Grabbed this way has difficulty speaking and must spend an extra action to perform any action that requires speaking, including casting spells.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/doppelganger-bb":{"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Doppelgangers can transform into perfect copies of other creatures but have indeterminate forms in their natural states.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"End the Charade","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the doppelganger is transformed with Change Shape and another creature moves adjacent to them or uses a Strike or another hostile action against them, the doppelganger can use its reaction to revert to its natural form and make a Strike against that creature.</p>\n<p>If the creature was unaware the doppelganger was in disguise, that creature has the Off-Guard condition against this Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The doppelganger takes on the specific appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid it has seen. This doesn't change the doppelganger's Stride speed or their attack and damage bonuses with their Strikes, but it might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).</p>"},{"n":"Mind Reading","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The doppelganger attempts to read the surface thoughts of one creature within 30 feet. The target resists if it succeeds at a DC 21 Will save.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/drow-priestess-bb":{"gear":["Hand Crossbow","Rapier","Shield","Chain Shirt","Religious Symbol (Wooden)","Bolts (10)"],"notes":{"ac":"22 with shield raised"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"Light Blindness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When first exposed to bright light, the drow Can't See until the end of their next turn. All squares are difficult terrain for them, and they take a -4 status penalty to Perception. If they try to attack a creature, the attack fails unless they succeed at a DC 11 Flat. Light doesn't blind them again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If she Raised a Shield since her last turn, the priestess can spend her reaction to block a Strike. Reduce the Strike's damage by 5, but then she and the shield both take the remaining damage, possibly Breaking or destroying the shield.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/drow-sneak-bb":{"lang":["Elven","Sakvroth"],"gear":["Hand Crossbow","Shortsword","Leather Armor","Bolts (10)"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Loners at heart, drow sneaks trust no one-least of all fellow drow. These drow rely on awareness and adaptation to survive the cutthroat nature of their society.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Light Blindness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When first exposed to bright light, the drow Can't See until the end of their next turn. All squares are difficult terrain for them, and they take a -4 status penalty to Perception. If they try to attack a creature, the attack fails unless they succeed at a DC 11 Flat. Light doesn't blind them again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Draw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The drow rogue draws a weapon using the Interact action, then Strikes with that weapon.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The drow sneak deals an extra 1d6 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/drow-warrior-bb":{"gear":["Hand Crossbow","Rapier","Dagger","Leather Armor","Bolts (10)"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Drow are the descendants of elves corrupted by a great evil when they fled deep underground long ago.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Light Blindness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When first exposed to bright light, the drow Can't See until the end of their next turn. All squares are difficult terrain for them, and they take a -4 status penalty to Perception. If they try to attack a creature, the attack fails unless they succeed at a DC 11 Flat. Light doesn't blind them again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Draw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The drow warrior draws a weapon using the Interact action, then Strikes with that weapon.</p>"},{"n":"Skewer","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The drow warrior Strikes with their rapier, and they gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the attack roll. If they succeed, the target takes 1d6 bleed.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/envenomed-lock-bb":{"description":"<p>A spring-loaded, poisoned spine is hidden near the keyhole of a lock. Disabling or breaking the trap doesn't disable or break the lock.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 17 Thievery on the spring mechanism</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spring","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature tries to unlock or Pick the Lock, a spine extends to attack that creature with a Spine attack.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/falling-ceiling-bb":{"disable":"<p>A hero must succeed at a DC 18 Thievery check on the triggering square or the ceiling to prevent the stone blocks from falling.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Falling Stones","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature steps on the square closest to the north door, the trap drops blocks of stone all along the hallway. It makes one ranged Strike against each creature between the two doors.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/falling-shelves":{"disable":"<p>A hero must succeed at a DC 18 Athletics or DC 18 Thievery check to prevent the shelves from collapsing.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Topple Over","a":"r","c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature attempts to touch the shelves or take anything from them, they collapse, sending debris throughout the room. The trap makes one melee Strike against each creature in the room.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/ferrous-butterfly-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Beautiful but deadly, the ferrous butterfly is a turkey-sized insectile creature bristling with dozens of gleaming, razor-edged blades. Considered harmless by most denizens of the Plane of Metal, they nonetheless pose a significant threat to organic creatures, whose iron-rich blood they find irresistible. The wing blades of these butterflies tend to break off during feeding and regrow naturally. These scales are reminiscent of jagged scraps of metal and can serve as surprisingly effective makeshift weapon.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"A Thousand Cuts","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A ferrous butterfly's knifelike wings cause terrible lacerations that continue to bleed. Any creature with persistent bleed damage from a ferrous butterfly's wing attack has weakness 2 to slashing damage until the bleeding is stopped.</p>\n<p>Effect: A Thousand Cuts</p>"},{"n":"Swoop","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ferrous butterfly Flies up to its Speed and makes a wing Strike at any point during that movement.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/forest-troll-bb":{"notes":{"hp":"regeneration 20 (deactivated by electricity or fire)"},"flavor":"<p>Forest trolls are dim-witted, gangly giants who stalk the fringes of civilization. They rely on their incredible strength to overpower foes with their vicious claws. A troll's endless hunger drives them to consume a variety of living creatures. Trolls stand anywhere from 12 to 16 feet tall, though they prefer to hunch to lull foes into a false sense of security.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Regeneration 20 (Deactivated by Electricity or Fire)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The troll regains 20 Hit Points at the start of their turn unless they've taken electricity or fire damage since their last turn. The troll can't die unless their regeneration is deactivated when they're reduced to 0 HP.</p>"},{"n":"Easily Misled","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The forest troll gets a –4 circumstance penalty to their Perception DC against deception checks.</p>"},{"n":"Rend","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the troll succeeds at two claw Strikes against the same creature in the same turn, they can use this ability to automatically deal claw Strike damage to that creature.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/gargoyle-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Gargoyles are monstrous hunters made entirely of stone. They look like decorative statues and use this as camouflage to hide in plain sight in cities during the day and descend upon unlucky pedestrians at night. Their most common form is that of a horned humanoid with batlike wings, but individual gargoyles vary greatly, with some appearing more or less humanoid and others resembling something else entirely. Gargoyles tend to be lone hunters, though sometimes they band into groups called wings.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Clawed Feet","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the gargoyle is flying and a creature moves into an adjacent square below them, the gargoyle can use their reaction to make a claw Strike against that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Statue","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>Until the next time they use an action, the gargoyle appears to be a statue. A creature must succeed at a DC 32 Perception check to figure out that the statue is really a creature.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/ghost-commoner-bb":{"notes":{"hp":"rejuvenation"},"abilities":[{"n":"Site Bound","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A ghost can stray no more than 120 feet from where it was killed or the place it haunts. Some are bound to items or creatures that were special to them rather than a location.</p>"},{"n":"Incorporeal","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A ghost has no body and can pass through physical objects, though it can't end its turn inside one. Most checks that use Strength and require a body, such as Grapple, don't work against a ghost, and a ghost can't attempt such checks.</p>"},{"n":"Rejuvenation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>Setting right the injustice that led to the ghost's death allows it to move on to the afterlife. Otherwise, when destroyed, the ghost re-forms after 2d4 days within the location it's bound to, fully healed.</p>"},{"n":"Frightful Moan","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Each living creature within 30 feet who hears the ghost must attempt a DC 21 Will save. On a failure, a creature gains the Frightened 2 condition (or Frightened 3 on a critical failure).</p>\n<p>On a success, a creature can't be affected by this ghost's Frightful Moan for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/ghoul-stalker-bb":{"flavor":"<p>The flesh-eating undead, known as ghouls, haunt sinister locations such as lonely graveyards and ruined crypts, making meals of corpses. Legends say that those captured by ghouls hear foul whispers that curse them into craving raw meat, eventually turning them into ghouls.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Stench","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that comes within 10 feet of the ghoul and can smell the ghoul must attempt a DC 14 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature takes a –1 status penalty to all checks and DCs until it uses an action to retch (Sickened 1). A creature that succeeds at its save isn't affected by any ghoul's stench for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Consume Flesh","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ghoul devours a chunk of a creature that died within the last hour and regains 1d6 healing Hit Points.</p>\n<p>The ghoul can regain Hit Points from a given body only once.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ghoul stalker deals an extra 1d4 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"},{"n":"Swift Leap","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ghoul jumps up to half its Speed. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/giant-ant-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Giant ants form vast underground colonies, excavating deep burrows or infesting existing caverns. Giant ants look identical to their smaller kin, but their size makes them a deadly threat to farms and travelers alike.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Giant Ant Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target that takes piercing damage from the giant ant's stinger Strike must succeed at a DC 18 Fortitude save or take 1d10 poison damage.</p>"},{"n":"Haul Away","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the giant ant has a creature Grabbed or Restrained with its mandibles, it can spend this action to Stride up to its speed, carrying the creature with it. At the end of the Stride, place the creature in any open square adjacent to the giant ant.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the ant succeeds at its mandibles Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the ant's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/giant-centipede-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Centipedes are relatively common arthropods that live, hunt, and scavenge amid dung and detritus. Scurrying about with surprising speed on the scores of legs attached to their long, segmented bodies, centipedes strike with poisoned mandibles.</p>\n<p>Most giant centipedes (known as sewer centipedes when found in cities) nest in small groups but hunt alone. Attempts to domesticate giant centipedes for use as guardians or pets generally end poorly, but some goblin and kobold societies have developed effective methods of utilizing these vermin as guardians. Some societies roast and eat centipedes, often with pungent peppers, as a savory delicacy. Care must be taken in preparing the meal, though, to avoid contaminating the flesh with the creature's venom.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Giant Centipede Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target that takes piercing damage from the centipede's mandibles Strike must succeed at a DC 14 Fortitude save or take 1d6 poison damage.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/giant-fly-bb":{"flavor":"<p>This massive fly's twitching limbs seem to never stop moving as it constantly cleans itself and scoops anything edible into its mouth parts. While primarily carrion eaters, giant flies sometimes prey on livestock or other animals too slow to get away. Left to their own devices, these flies will lay dozens of eggs within the mostly-eaten carcasses. These eggs soon hatch into enormous maggots that begin the cycle of scavenging anew.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Avoid the Swat","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The giant fly is targeted with a melee or ranged attack by an attacker it can see</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The giant fly gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the attack misses, the giant insect can Fly up to its fly Speed.</p>"},{"n":"Fly Pox","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease"],"f":"","d":"<p>A giant fly could carry any disease, but most transmit an infection called fly pox with their bite. A character who is critically hit by a giant fly's mandibles must succeed at a DC 16 Fortitude saving throw or be Enfeebled 1 for 1 day.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/giant-rat-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Giant rats are enormous versions of the common vermin. They're typically found in abundant numbers, but since they can't fit in the nooks where ordinary rats typically hide, they're much easier to locate and exterminate. In fact, finding and slaying a giant rat is a rite of passage for many an adventurer. Such tasks get tiresome quickly, so many veterans subcontract extermination to new adventurers.</p>\n<p>Giant rats mostly live in sewers where they can scavenge from the streets above, but some families of giant rats live in more remote locations, such as dank caves, forests, or hills. Rats are incredibly adept survivors and can be found nearly anywhere in the world, though they tend to favor temperate or warm climates as opposed to cold regions.</p>\n<p>Although their bite alone isn't lethal except to the very weak, some giant rats carry a dangerous disease common to rodents around the world—a pestilence more than capable of ravaging rural communities. The rats are merely carriers with no risk of succumbing to the disease themselves.</p>"},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/giant-spider-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Few everyday vermin inspire as much dread as the infamous spider. Giant spiders vary in size. The human-sized versions, sometimes called hunting spiders, are the most common type of giant spider, though not the largest.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Descend on a Web","a":"1","c":"interaction","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The giant spider moves straight down up to 40 feet, suspended by a web line. It can hang from the web or drop off. The distance it Descends on a Web doesn't count for falling damage. A creature can Strike the web, which has AC 20 and 8 HP. If the web is reduced to 0 HP, the spider falls.</p>"},{"n":"Giant Spider Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target damaged by the spider's fangs must succeed at a DC 16 Fortitude save or take 1d10 poison damage and gain the Off-Guard condition for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Web Trap","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by the giant spider's web Strike gets stuck to the nearest surface. It can't move until it successfully Escapes.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/giant-viper-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Snakes come in an array of forms, from jungle-dwelling constrictors that wrap around their prey to venomous vipers with deadly bites. Regardless, all snakes consume prey whole by stretching their lower jaw and using powerful muscles to move the food down their throats and into their stomachs.</p>\n<p>The giant viper's fangs, nearly as long as daggers, easily inspire fear. The venom injected by a giant viper can cause severe blood clotting and inflict tremendous damage.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Coiled Opportunity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the giant viper is Coiled and a creature moves into or through a square adjacent to it, the giant viper can use its reaction to make a fangs Strike against that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Coil","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The giant viper uses an action to coil itself. While coiled, it can target a creature up to 10 feet away with its fangs Strike. After the giant viper Strikes with its fangs, it becomes uncoiled</p>"},{"n":"Giant Viper Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target damaged by the snake's fangs must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or take 1d8 poison damage.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/goblin-commando-bb":{"gear":["Greatsword","Shortbow","Leather Armor","Arrows (20)"],"flavor":"<p>Most goblin communities teeter in a state of barely controlled disarray—a collective of creatures operating largely on gut instinct rarely follows any clear direction. Even goblin leaders tend to be impulsive, irresponsible, and generally just not that good at actually leading.</p>\n<p>In theory, goblin commandos lead goblin raids. In practice, goblin commandos rarely continue to lead their comrades once a battle has begun. Most shirk their responsibilities in favor of wading into the fray and claiming glory from their kin.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Goblin Scuttle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a goblin ally ends a move action adjacent to the goblin commando, the commando can use their reaction to Step.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/goblin-igniter-bb":{"lore":[["Fire Lore",7]],"gear":["Torch"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Goblins find fire totally fascinating. It makes light. It's great for cooking. It's a fun toy! Some goblins take their people's admiration of fire a little bit too far and into the realm of deadly obsession.</p>\n<p>Goblins who turn their attention to magic so they can learn to make fire from nothing are known as goblin igniters. These flame fanatics can be a great boon to a band of goblin raiders eager to torch their enemies and wreak havoc. More often, however, their presence is a double-edged sword. In the heat of the moment, goblin igniters sometimes lose sight of their goals and simply set fire to anything that will burn—including their own allies!</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Goblin Scuttle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a goblin ally ends a move action adjacent to the goblin igniter, the igniter can use their reaction to Step.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/goblin-warrior-bb":{"gear":["Shortbow","Shortsword","Leather Armor","Arrows (10)"],"flavor":"<p>The frontline fighters of goblin tribes prefer to fight in large groups—especially when they can outnumber their foes by at least three to one. One doesn't need intense training or great toughness to become a goblin warrior. Anyone can aspire to this role, or be drafted into it during an emergency.</p>\n<p>Goblin warriors delight in wreaking havoc. They think nothing of slaughtering livestock, stealing infants, or burning down buildings purely for momentary delight. They revel in playing malicious tricks on taller humanoids, whom they call \"longshanks.\" What the goblins lack in consistency, long-term planning, and good sense, they make up for in sheer bravery and commitment.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Goblin Scuttle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a goblin ally ends a move action adjacent to the goblin warrior, the warrior can use their reaction to Step.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/harpy-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Harpies are an amalgamation of human and bird, using their ancestral control of the wind to lure prey or even directly pull in their next meal. Harpies can eat most creatures, but prefer to eat humans and elves in particular. Harpies live in family groups or larger clans, although they rarely hunt in big groups, preferring to keep most meals for themselves.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Stench","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that comes within 30 feet of the harpy and can smell the harpy must attempt a DC 21 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature takes a –1 status penalty to all checks and DCs until it uses an action to retch (Sickened 1). A creature that succeeds at its save isn't affected by any harpy's stenches for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Hungry Winds","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The harpy uses the wind to pull its prey closer. A target within 20 feet must succeed at a DC 21 Fortitude save or be pulled adjacent to the harpy. The harpy then makes a jaws strike against the target. If the target is pulled into the air and cannot fly, it falls as normal.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/hell-hound-bb":{"lang":["Diabolic","(can't speak)"],"flavor":"<p>Temperamental and quick to aggressive behavior, hell hounds are fiendish canines from a hellish plane. They're skilled hunters and can breathe gouts of flame from their maws. A hell hound's appearance leaves no doubts as to its infernal origins—flesh the color of burning pitch, teeth as sharp as any fiend's pitchfork, and a shroud of ever-burning hellfire are all trademark features. Though they can't speak, they understand Diabolic, the language of Hell.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Hellfire Breath","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hell hound breathes flames that deal 4d6 fire damage to all creatures in a 15-foot cone. Each affected creature must attempt a DC 19 basic Reflex save.</p>\n<p>The hell hound can't use Hellfire Breath again for 1d4 rounds. If the hell hound would take fire damage or is the target of a fire effect, its Hellfire Breath recharges.</p>"},{"n":"Pack Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hell hound's jaws Strike deals 1d4 extra damage to creatures within reach of two of the hell hounds' allies.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/hidden-pit-bb":{"description":"<p>A wooden trapdoor covers a 10-foot square pit that's 20 feet deep.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 12 Thievery to remove the trapdoor.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(or DC 0 Perception if the trapdoor is disabled or broken)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Pitfall","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a creature walks onto the trap door, that creature falls in unless it succeeds at a Reflex save to grab hold of the edge. The pit is 20 feet deep, dealing 10 bludgeoning damage to anyone who falls to the bottom.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/hobgoblin-archer-bb":{"gear":["Crossbow","Shortsword","Scale Mail","Bolts (20)"],"flavor":"<p>Bands of hobgoblin soldiers typically have at least one archer among their ranks. In smaller groups, the hobgoblin archer also serves as that band's captain. These archers generally command these groups from a distance or higher ground and they make use of their keen senses to watch for strategic openings.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Formation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When they're adjacent to at least two other allies, the hobgoblin archer gains a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and saving throws.</p>"},{"n":"Crossbow Precision","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first time the archer hits with a crossbow attack in a round, they deal 1d8 extra precision damage.</p>"},{"n":"Running Reload","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The archer Strides, Steps, or Sneaks, then Interacts to reload.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/hobgoblin-soldier-bb":{"gear":["Longsword","Shortbow","Shield","Breastplate","Arrows (10)"],"notes":{"ac":"(20 with shield raised)"},"flavor":"<p>Hobgoblins are devoted to war, and their entire civilization is built upon fostering and maintaining conflict while proving their battle superiority. Highly organized, they work efficiently in groups, whether that group is a small raiding party, a roving war band, or a fully regimented army. Physically, hobgoblins stand about as tall as humans and have gray, ashen skin.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Formation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When they're adjacent to at least two other allies, the hobgoblin soldier gains a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and saving throws.</p>"},{"n":"Raise a Shield","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hobgoblin soldier lifts up their shield to get a +2 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of their next turn</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If they Raised a Shield since their last turn, the hobgoblin can spend their reaction to block a Strike. Reduce the damage by 5, but the hobgoblin and the shield both take the remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/horned-dragon-juvenile-bb":{"abilities":[{"n":"Twisting Tail","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature within 10 feet uses a move action or leaves a square during a move action it's using, the dragon can use their reaction to make a tail Strike at the creature with a –2 penalty. If it hits, the creature stops moving in the square it was in when the dragon used this reaction.</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Frenzy","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragon makes two claw Strikes and one tail Strike in any order.</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Momentum","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the dragon gets a critical success on a Strike, they recharge their Poison Breath.</p>"},{"n":"Poison Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragon breathes a toxic cloud that deals 5d6 poison damage in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 21 basic Reflex save. The dragon can't use Poison Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-boss-zolgran-bb":{"lang":["Draconic"],"lore":[["Dragon Lore",10]],"gear":["Staff","Eggshell Necklace","Iron Key"],"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Zolgran deals an extra 1d6 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-mage-black-bb":{"lore":[["Dragon Lore",10]],"gear":["Staff"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Kobolds are small, reptilian humanoids who are often seen in the service of more powerful creatures. They lurk in dark places, usually tunnels and mines. Kobold mages use magic to carry out their schemes, often in service of a dragon or other powerful creatures.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-mage-blue-bb":{"lore":[["Dragon Lore",10]],"gear":["Staff"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Kobolds are small, reptilian humanoids who are often seen in the service of more powerful creatures. They lurk in dark places, usually tunnels and mines. Kobold mages use magic to carry out their schemes, often in service of a dragon or other powerful creatures.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-mage-green-bb":{"lore":[["Dragon Lore",10]],"gear":["Staff"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Kobolds are small, reptilian humanoids who are often seen in the service of more powerful creatures. They lurk in dark places, usually tunnels and mines. Kobold mages use magic to carry out their schemes, often in service of a dragon or other powerful creatures.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-mage-red-bb":{"lore":[["Dragon Lore",10]],"gear":["Staff"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Kobolds are small, reptilian humanoids who are often seen in the service of more powerful creatures. They lurk in dark places, usually tunnels and mines. Kobold mages use magic to carry out their schemes, often in service of a dragon or other powerful creatures.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-mage-white-bb":{"lore":[["Dragon Lore",10]],"gear":["Staff"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Kobolds are small, reptilian humanoids who are often seen in the service of more powerful creatures. They lurk in dark places, usually tunnels and mines. Kobold mages use magic to carry out their schemes, often in service of a dragon or other powerful creatures.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-scout-bb":{"gear":["Crossbow","Shortsword","Leather Armor","Bolts (20)"],"flavor":"<p>Most kobolds encountered outside of a well-defended warren or lair are kobold scouts, trained for stalking and the hunt. They're charged with bringing food and valuable goods back to the community. Kobolds are skilled at working together by necessity, and they often set up ambushes or hit-and-run assaults that allow them to do the most damage possible without putting themselves at much risk.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kobold scout deals an extra 1d6 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-trapmaster-bb":{"gear":["Shortsword","Spear (3)","Leather Armor","Spike Trap"],"flavor":"<p>Kobold trapmasters are the masterminds behind crafting and implementing wily traps in kobold lairs, and are widely respected among their kind.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Quick Trap","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kobold trapmaster deploys one of their spike traps in an adjacent square.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Once this trap is deployed in a square, it deals 2d8 piercing damage to anyone who steps on that square and they must attempt a DC 17 basic Reflex saving throw. A hero takes no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, full damage on a failure, and double damage on a critical failure. These traps can be disabled with a successful DC 15 Thievery check.</p>"},{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kobold trapmaster deals an extra 1d6 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/kobold-warrior-bb":{"gear":["Spear","Leather Armor"],"flavor":"<p>A typical kobold trains with simple weaponry. Kobolds are capable of landing sneaky strikes against unsuspecting foes, but they're just as quick to scamper off to safety if their group wouldn't outnumber their enemies by at least two to one.</p>\n<p>Kobolds believe in pragmatism, and a defeated kobold would rather surrender than face death. One might even abandon their kobold kin and concede to serve the victor if the alternative is an untimely demise.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Scamper","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the kobold is adjacent to at least one enemy, the kobold Strides up to 30 feet and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against reactions triggered by this movement. The kobold must end this movement in a space that's not adjacent to any enemy.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kobold warrior deals an extra 1d4 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/leopard-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Leopards range from the iconic yellow with black spots to black panthers and white-furred snow leopards. Few predators can match their talent for stalking and stealth.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Maul","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The leopard makes two claw Strikes against a creature it has Grabbed or Restrained. The second attack uses the same multiple attack penalty as the first, but later attacks that turn take a –10 multiple attack penalty (or –8 for its claws).</p>"},{"n":"Pounce","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The leopard Strides and makes a Strike at the end of that movement. If the leopard successfully used Hide before this action, the target has the Off-Guard condition against this Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The leopard deals an extra 1d4 damage to creatures that have the Off-Guard condition.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the leopard succeeds at its jaws Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the leopard's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/lukahn":{"abilities":[{"n":"Incorporeal","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Lukahn has no body and can pass through physical objects, though he can't end his turn inside one. Most checks that use Strength and require a body, such as Grapple and Shove, don't work against Lukahn, and he can't use them.</p>"},{"n":"Light Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Attacks against Lukahn are treated as magical if he or the weapon being used against him is in light.</p>"},{"n":"Shadow Veil","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Lukahn is targeted by a melee attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Lukahn gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/magnetic-skink":{"flavor":"<p>The scales of these large lizards are magnetic, drawing scraps of metal to their bodies. In addition to eating insects and other small prey, magnetic skinks also feed on small amounts of metal, so they're known to reside near settlements with access to these materials.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Uncanny Climber","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A magnetic skink's feet allow it to climb virtually any surface, no matter how slick or sheer. If a skink attempts an Athletics check to Climb and critically fails, it gets a failure instead.</p>"},{"n":"Launch Metal","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The skink repulses the metal attached to its body in all directions, dealing 2d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 15 basic Reflex save) to all creatures adjacent to the skink. The skink can't use Launch Metal again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Unsteadying Magnetism","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The skink amplifies its magnetic field and tries to pull the metal away from a creature within 20 feet. If that creature is wearing metal armor or holding a metal item, they must attempt a DC 15 Fortitude save. On a failure, that creature is Off-Guard until the start of the skink's next turn.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/mermaid-fountain-bb":{"disable":"<p>DC 20 Thievery on each corner mechanism (must disable all three working corners to disable the trap)</p>\n<p>Each corner mechanism has hardness 8 and 15 HP</p>","routine":"<p>Each turn, the fountain uses 1 action. Roll a 1d10 and look up the result on the following list to determine which action it uses that round.</p><ul><li><strong>1-4 Single Target</strong> The statue spins about and sprays water at a single random target in the room. Roll a 1d4 and count to the number you rolled, starting with the player on your left, to determine which hero gets attacked. The spray is a ranged Strike.</li><li><strong>5-7 Corner Spray</strong> The statue spins about, firing a spray of water at each corner of the room that still has a functioning corner mechanism. This hits any creature adjacent to the corner mechanism, dealing 2d6 bludgeoning damage. Each hero must attempt a DC 15 basic Reflex, taking no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, full damage on a failure, and double damage on a critical failure.</li><li><strong>8-9 Half Room</strong> The statue spins about, spraying half of the room with water. Roll any die. If the result is even, it sprays the west half; otherwise, it sprays the east half. This deals 2d6 bludgeoning damage to each creature in that half of the room, and each hero must attempt a DC 15 basic Reflex save.</li><li><strong>10 Full Room</strong> This works just like the half-room attack, but it targets everyone in the room.</li></ul>","stealthNote":"<p><strong>Notice</strong> DC 20 Perception check</p>"},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/mimic-bb":{"lang":["Common"],"flavor":"<p>Thought to be the result of a failed experiment meant to animate objects or a sinister alghollthu creation, mimics are clever monsters that can take the form of common manufactured objects. Mimics are ambush predators and voracious eaters, surprising their prey through their uncanny ability to mimic the form of common furniture and miscellany. They remain disguised until unsuspecting adventurers happen by, then they lash out in ambush.</p>\n<p>Mimics possess complex alien minds, and while often cruel and self-serving, they also enjoy conversation with their prey from time to time. For unknown reasons, they are especially interested in humanoids. Mimics have a strong dislike for others of their kind and tend to live alone. A mimic can remain in its alternate form for an extremely long period of time, sometimes remaining disguised in a dungeon chamber for decades. Regardless of how long it waits, the mimic remains vigilant and alert, ready to strike at any moment.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Adhesive","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Any creature that touches the mimic (usually from a fist Strike, the mimic's pseudopod, or a Grapple or Shove) must succeed at a DC 23 Reflex save or gain the Grabbed condition. The DC to Escape is 23. A melee or thrown weapon that hits the mimic sticks to it. A character can spend an action to attempt a DC 23 Athletics check, removing the weapon on a success. The adhesive dissolves 1 minute after the mimic dies.</p>"},{"n":"Object Lesson","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a creature touches the mimic while the mimic is transformed into an object, the mimic can spend its reaction to use its adhesive with no saving throw. The mimic then makes a pseudopod Strike. Object Lesson can't be used again until the mimic escapes and takes on a new disguise.</p>"},{"n":"Mimic Object","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The mimic assumes the shape of any Medium object. This alters its visual appearance but not its size. It takes a DC 28 Perception check to tell the object is a creature.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/minotaur-hunter-bb":{"gear":["Greataxe"],"flavor":"<p>A minotaur is a large humanoid with a bovine head and hooves. Though often mistaken for aggressive brutes, many minotaurs are skilled artisans. Lone minotaurs tend to make their lairs within a maze or old ruin, hunting anyone who dares to invade their labyrinthine home.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Perfect Orienteering","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A minotaur automatically critically succeeds on Survival checks to Sense direction or Track</p>"},{"n":"Axe Swipe","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The minotaur makes two Strikes with their greataxe against two adjacent enemies, both of whom are within their reach. The second attack uses the same multiple attack penalty as the first, but attacks they make after this take a –10 multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Powerful Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The minotaur Strides twice, then makes a horn Strike. If they moved at least 20 feet from their starting position, the Strike's damage is increased to 2d8+10.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/ogre-warrior-bb":{"gear":["Javelin (6)","Greataxe","Hide Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Ogres embody cruel greed and brutish, amoral violence. Standing 10 feet tall and densely muscled, ogres are as strong as they are vicious. They typically enjoy remorseless violence in all of its forms. Although they prefer to vent their violent urges on smaller humanoids—the smaller, the better—ogres promise a horrifying fate for anyone unlucky enough to fall within their meaty grasp.</p>\n<p>Always eager for mayhem and murder, ogre warriors are quick to turn on their kin when there's a shortage of smaller folk to torment, so those who lead ogres do their best to keep them constantly distracted with new opportunities for raids and ruin. An ogre's deficits in both patience and intelligence make them easy to trick, giving cunning captives many ways to get the better of them.</p>"},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/orc-commander-bb":{"gear":["Javelin (6)","Maul","Hide Armor"],"flavor":"<p>When orcs raid, the strongest is chosen as the leader. Bonds of blood are especially strong among orcs and the mightiest orc holds are typically made up of siblings who have chosen a strong commander to protect their kinfolk.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the orc is reduced to 0 Hit Points, they can use their reaction to remain conscious with 1 Hit Point, but they gain the Wounded 1 condition (or increases the wounded value by 1 if they already have that condition). The orc can't use this ability at wounded 3.</p>"},{"n":"Battle Cry","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Bellowing mightily, the commander gives themself and all orc allies within 60 feet who can hear them a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls until the start of the orc commander's next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: Battle Cry</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/orc-scrapper-bb":{"gear":["Javelin (3)","Battle Axe","Hide Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Orcs are proud, strong humanoids that live by the rule that might makes right. They amass in warbands both large and small, conquering territory and robbing those unlucky enough to cross their path. Countless small settlements, outposts, and forts have fallen at the hands of orc raiders, whose sheer destructiveness leaves an indelible mark on the lands they conquer. The furious and undisciplined rank-and-file scrappers make up the bulk of an orc warband.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the orc is reduced to 0 Hit Points, they can use their reaction to remain conscious with 1 Hit Point, but they gain the Wounded 1 condition (or increases the wounded value by 1 if they already have that condition). The orc can't use this ability at wounded 3.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/orc-veteran-bb":{"gear":["Javelin (4)","Shortsword (2)","Battle Axe","Breastplate"],"flavor":"<p>The typical orc trooper is a violent combatant familiar to many adventurers. Orc warriors fight for their holds, for riches, and—perhaps most of all—for glory. Proving their own strength improves their station within their orc hold, so battle is a crucial part of life for any orc who aspires to one day lead or go down in history.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the orc is reduced to 0 Hit Points, they can use their reaction to remain conscious with 1 Hit Point, but they gain the Wounded 1 condition (or increases the wounded value by 1 if they already have that condition). The orc can't use this ability at wounded 3.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/owlbear-bb":{"flavor":"<p>The owlbear is a territorial predator with the body of a brown bear but the head-and resultant keen senses-of an owl.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Bloodcurdling Screech","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Each creature within 80 feet who can hear the owlbear's screech must attempt a DC 20 Will save. The creatures can't be affected by another screech for 1 minute. On a critical success, the creature is unaffected; on a success, the creature gains the Frightened 1 condition; on a failure, the creature gains the Frightened 2 condition; on a critical failure, the creature gains the Frightened 3 condition and must spend its next turn running away from the owlbear.</p>"},{"n":"Screeching Advance","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The owlbear makes a Bloodcurdling Screech and Strides twice. All creatures within 80 feet of the owlbear at any point during this movement are subjected to the effects of Bloodcurdling Screech.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the owlbear succeeds at its talon Strike, it can use this action immediately after to automatically give the target the Grabbed condition until the end of its next turn.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/pugwampi-bb":{"gear":["Shortbow","Shortsword","Arrows (60)"],"notes":{"per":"(-2 to hear things)"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Gremlins are cruel fey tricksters and saboteurs who enjoy causing inventive destructiveness. Dog-faced pugwampis are craven, and they take great joy in the accidents and missteps caused by the ill fortune they magically project.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"-2 Penalty on Perception to Hear things","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Animal Talker","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Pugwampis can talk to and understand animals.</p>"},{"n":"Unluck Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Creatures other than animals, gremlins, and kholo within 20 feet become extremely unlucky. They must attempt a DC 16 Will save, rolling this Will save twice and using the worse result.</p>\n<p>On a successful save, the creature can't be affected by pugwampi unluck auras for 24 hours. On a failure, the creature must roll twice and use the worse result on all checks as long as it's within 20 feet of the pugwampi.</p>\n<p>Multiple pugwampis don't create any increased effect.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/reefclaw-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Reefclaws are aquatic monsters that resemble huge shrimp or lobsters. Though reefclaws can't speak, they are intelligent enough to understand the local language of humanoids near their hunting grounds.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Death Frenzy","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the reefclaw is reduced to 0 hit points it can spend this reaction to make a claw Strike before dying.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the reefclaw has a creature Grabbed or Restrained, it can spend one action to crush them in its coils. The creature takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage depending on its DC 17 basic Fortitude save.</p>"},{"n":"Reefclaw Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target that takes slashing damage from the reefclaw's claw Strike must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or take 1d6 poison damage.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the reeflclaw succeeds at its claw Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the reefclaw's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/scythe-blades-bb":{"description":"<p>Two blades, each hidden in a 15-foot-long ceiling groove, are both connected to a trip wire.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 21 Thievery to disable each blade.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Falling Scythes","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the trip wire is pulled or severed, both blades swing down, each one attacking all creatures under the ceiling grooves. The trap makes a melee attack with each blade with +17 to each attack roll. There's no multiple attack penalty on these attacks. On a hit, a blade deals 2d12+4 slashing damage. On a critical hit, the damage is doubled plus 6 extra damage.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Scythe":"<p>No multiple attack penalty</p>"}},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/sea-hag-bb":{"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Hags are malevolent predators who use magic and manipulation to lure children and young adults into their clutches. They seek out targets who are unhappy, innocent, or otherwise vulnerable, preying on their weaknesses before snatching them up. A sea hag has the upper half of a humanoid and the lower half of an octopus, with translucent skin and glowing lights visible beneath their flesh.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Dread Gaze","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hag gazes upon a creature, afflicting it with a gnawing sense of impending doom, with a result depending on its DC 20 Will save. The target doesn't need to be able to see the sea hag.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is frightened 1 and is Slowed 1 for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is Frightened 2 and slowed 1 for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/severed-head-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Severed heads are the reanimated heads of decapitation victims. These mindless undead fly through the air or roll around to attack their prey. In addition to attacking the living like other undead, severed heads can sometimes be drawn to things important to them in life. Scholars argue that this is likely due to particularly powerful thoughts that can break through momentarily in what's left of a severed head's mind. Unfortunately, their mindless state prevents them from recognizing their goal, and they remain violent even after encountering what they seek.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Gnash","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the severed head succeeds at its jaws Strike, it can use this action immediately after to make a second jaws Strike at the same target as it violently shakes itself, trying to rip away a mouthful of flesh. On a success, the target takes an additional 1d4 slashing damage and 1 persistent bleed damage.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/sewer-ooze-bb":{"flavor":"<p>These amorphous masses of sewage and detritus make their way through filthy culverts beneath cities. Some grow to enormous sizes and have insatiable appetites.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Motion Sense 60 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A sewer ooze can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement, allowing it to fight as well as if it could see. However, a sewer ooze can't see, so effects that depend on vision or seeing don't work on it.</p>"},{"n":"Filth Wave","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sewer ooze unleashes a wave of filth, covering all creatures within 20 feet of itself. Each creature in the area must succeed at a DC 17 Reflex save or take 1d4 acid damage and a –10-foot penalty to its Speeds for 1 minute (on a critical failure, the creature also falls over and gains the Prone condition). A creature can Interact to clean someone off. This decreases the Speed penalty to -5 feet after 1 action, or to no penalty after 2 actions. After using Filth Wave, the ooze can't use it again for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>Effect: Filth Wave</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shadow-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Undead shadows feed on those who stray from the light.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Incorporeal","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A shadow has no body and can pass through physical objects, though it can't end its turn inside one. Most checks that use Strength and require a body, such as Grapple and Shove, don't work against a shadow, and a shadow can't use them.</p>"},{"n":"Light Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Attacks against the shadow are treated as magical if the shadow or the weapon being used is in light.</p>"},{"n":"Slink in Shadows","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadow can Hide or end its Sneak in a creature's or object's shadow.</p>"},{"n":"Steal Shadow","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>If the shadow hits a living creature with a Strike on its previous action, it can use this action to pull at the target's shadow, imposing a –1 status penalty to Athletics and to attack rolls and damage rolls that use Strength (Enfeebled 1). The penalty increases each time a shadow uses this ability to a maximum of –4. The penalty decreases by 1 every hour.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shadow-bat":{"flavor":"<p>The shadowy magical energies related to some wicked deities, evil forces, or the shadowy plane of existence called the Netherworld sometimes manifest in the form of corrupted living creatures. The shadow bat has the physique of a giant bat made of shadows with the magical ability to create powerful gusts of wind.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Echolocation","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The bat can \"see\" using its hearing at the listed range, allowing it to function just as well in darkness.</p>"},{"n":"Screeching Gust","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadow bat flaps its wings and lets out a mighty screech, creating a cone of tearing winds and piercing sound. All creatures in a 15-foot cone take 3d6 sonic damage, with a DC 16 basic Reflex saving throw. Creatures that fail are pushed backwards 10 feet by the wind.</p>\n<p>Using its wings in this way exhausts the shadow bat, causing it to fall harmlessly to the ground immediately after using this ability and preventing it from taking flight or using Screeching Gust again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shadow-gargoyle":{"abilities":[{"n":"Clawed Feet","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the gargoyle is flying and a creature moves into an adjacent square below them, the gargoyle can use their reaction to make a claw Strike against that creature.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shadow-priest":{"flavor":"<p>Sometimes, followers of unholy deities will transform into shadows upon their death, a gift from their wicked patrons.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Incorporeal","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadow priest has no body and can pass through physical objects, though they can't end their turn inside one. Most checks that use Strength and require a body, such as Grapple and Shove, don't work against the shadow priest, and the shadow priest can't use them.</p>"},{"n":"Light Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Attacks against the shadow priest are treated as magical if the shadow priest or the weapon being used against them is in light.</p>"},{"n":"Shadow Veil","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the shadow priest is targeted by a melee attack, they can use their reaction to gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shadow-twigjack":{"flavor":"<p>\"True\" twigjacks, as they consider themselves, are found in wild forests alongside the fey they idolize.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Maladjusted forest denizens, twigjacks form from the cruel and prankish combination of fey and the very woods in which they reside. A twigjack's body is made up of prickly brambles woven with vines. Shaggy, mossy growth, not unlike hair, tops a twigjack's head. Its mouth is just a canyon of splintered and broken sticks bisecting its face. Leaves and sprigs of new growth randomly sprout from the creature's body. Many dense forests on Golarion have at least a handful of twigjacks living in the undergrowth.</p>\n<p>While truculent and violent, twigjacks care deeply for what they consider to be their forests. These creatures harass outsiders who delve deep into their wooded domains, forcing back even the most determined explorers, foresters, and travelers, especially when those intruders cut roads through the forest. However, they are not terribly territorial when it comes to other forest creatures. When sylvan creatures, especially fey, rally against an outside threat, twigjacks in the area eagerly arrive to fight, even if they were not invited.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Bramble Jump","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["plant","primal","teleportation","wood"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the twigjack is in undergrowth, it can instantly teleport to a square of undergrowth within 60 feet. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Splinter Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The twigjack sprays a barrage of splinters and brambles from its body that deals 3d6 piercing damage in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 18 basic Reflex save. The twigjack can't use Splinter Spray again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shadow-walls":{"disable":"<p>DC 20 Arcana, DC 20 Nature, DC 20 Occultism, or DC 20 Religion on each of the shadow walls (disabling three of the four walls ends the hazard), or activating the orrery with the <em>unlit star</em> as noted in \"The Orrery of Light.\"</p>","routine":"<p>Each turn, the walls use 1 action. Roll a d10 and look up the result on the following list to determine which action the walls uses that round.</p><p><strong>1–4 Single Target</strong> The walls lash out at a random hero in the room. Roll a d4 and count to the number you rolled, starting with the player on your left, to determine which hero gets attacked. The shadow lash is a ranged Strike with +10 to hit. On a hit, it deals 2d6 void damage (doubled on a critical hit as normal).</p><p><strong>5–7 Wall Barrage</strong> The shadow arms lunge out from their respective wall, assaulting any one near an active wall. This hits any creature within 10 feet of an active wall (within 10 feet of a shadow hand on the map), dealing 2d6 void damage. Each hero must attempt a DC 15 basic Reflex save, taking no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, full damage on a failure, and double damage on a critical failure.</p><p><strong>8–9 Split Assault</strong> The shadows lash out against one half of the room. Roll any die. If the result is even, they assault the western half; otherwise, they assault the eastern half. This deals 2d6 void damage to each creature in that half of the room, and each hero must attempt a DC 15 basic Reflex save.</p><p><strong>10 Overwhelming Assault</strong> Like the split assault attack, but it targets everyone in the room.</p>","strikeNotes":{"Shadow Lash":"<p><em>Note: This Strike can only be used with the <strong>Single Target</strong> result of the Shadow Walls' routine.</em></p>"}},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/shulzara":{"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Hags are malevolent predators who use magic and manipulation to lure children and young adults into their clutches. They seek out targets who are unhappy, innocent, or otherwise vulnerable, preying on their weaknesses before snatching them up. A sea hag has the upper half of a humanoid and the lower half of an octopus, with translucent skin and glowing lights visible beneath their flesh.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Slithering Steps","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Shulzara is not affected by difficult terrain due to water.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/skeletal-giant-bb":{"gear":["Greataxe","Half Plate"],"flavor":"<p>The reanimated bones of giants make excellent necromantic thralls, and the skeletal giants made out of bull-headed minotaurs are no exception. Mindless skeletons use similar tactics, so using a bigger, more durable skeleton is the only way a necromancer can obtain a more powerful thrall.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Broad Swipe","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The skeletal giant makes two Strikes with its greataxe against two adjacent foes, both of whom are within its reach. The second attack uses the same multiple attack penalty as the first, but attacks it makes after this take a -10 multiple attack penalty (or a -8 multiple attack penalty for its horns).</p>"},{"n":"Terrifying Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The giant Strides and makes a horns Strike with a +4 circumstance bonus to damage.</p>\n<p>If the strike hits, the giant attempts to Demoralize the target.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/skeleton-guard-bb":{"gear":["Scimitar","Shortbow","Arrows (20)"],"flavor":"<p>Made from bones held together by foul necromancy, skeletons can often be found haunting old dungeons and patrolling forgotten cemeteries. Many evil masterminds prefer to keep eternally vigilant undead as minions to avoid the upkeep required to feed and satisfy the psychological needs of living guardians.</p>\n<p>Simple skeleton guards remain the most common skeletal minions. These skeletons are mindless, meaning they can't truly reason but can execute their basic guard duties of watching out for and attacking intruders. A group of several skeletons defending the same location usually consists of melee fighters and archers who shoot arrows from afar.</p>"},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/slamming-door-bb":{"description":"<p>Pressure-sensitive panels in the floor connect to a stone slab hidden in a hallway's ceiling.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 15 Thievery on the floor panels before the slab falls.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Slam Shut","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When pressure is placed on a floor tile, the door falls, closing off the hallway. The stone slab deals 3d8 bludgeoning damage to anyone beneath or adjacent to the slab when it drops and pushes them out of its space in a random direction. A creature that succeeds at a DC 17 Reflex save takes no damage and rolls out of the way in a random direction. On a critical success, they roll out of the way and can choose which direction. Lifting the fallen slab requires a successful DC 25 Athletics check. Hitting the floor panels triggers the trap. The slab uses the same AC and saves as the trap, but it has Hardness 12, HP 48 (BT 24).</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/sod-hound-bb":{"notes":{"per":"crystal sense 60 feet"},"flavor":"<p>Earth elementals such as sod hounds make excellent bodyguards for spelunkers and are ideal protectors of important subterranean locations. Coming from the Plane of Earth, they often appear in caverns deep underground.</p>\n<p>Sod hounds take the form of mossy canines made of packed dirt and pebbles. They can band together with other sod hounds, traveling as a pack.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Crystal Sense 60 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A sod hound can sense crystals or gems within 60 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Earth Glide","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sod hound burrows through any earthen matter, including rock. It moves up to 20 feet, leaving no tunnels or signs of its passing.</p>"},{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the sod hound succeeds at its jaws Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Trip the target. This Trip doesn't apply or count toward the sod hound's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/spear-launcher-bb":{"description":"<p>A wall socket loaded with a spear connects to a floor tile in one 5-foot square.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Thievery on the floor tile or wall socket.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spear","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>When pressure is applied to the floor tile, the trap shoots a spear, making an attack against the creature or object on the floor tile. The trap makes a ranged Spear attack.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/string-slime-bb":{"abilities":[{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A string slime can feel nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Split","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a string slime would take slashing damage (if it weren't immune) and has at least 10 Hit Points, it splits into two identical slimes with half the original's Hit Points. One string slime is in the same space as the original, and the other appears in an adjacent unoccupied space. If no adjacent space is unoccupied, move smaller creatures and objects out of the way to make a space or the split is canceled at the GM's discretion.</p>"},{"n":"Tag Team","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The slime arcs acidic protoplasm to another string slime within 30 feet along a straight line. Each creature in that line takes 3d6 acid damage with a DC 16 basic Reflex save. A creature that fails its save is also knocked Prone.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/twigjack-bb":{"flavor":"<p>\"True\" twigjacks, as they consider themselves, are found in wild forests alongside the fey they idolize.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Maladjusted forest denizens, twigjacks form from the cruel and prankish combination of fey and the very woods in which they reside. A twigjack's body is made up of prickly brambles woven with vines. Shaggy, mossy growth, not unlike hair, tops a twigjack's head. Its mouth is just a canyon of splintered and broken sticks bisecting its face. Leaves and sprigs of new growth randomly sprout from the creature's body. Many dense forests on Golarion have at least a handful of twigjacks living in the undergrowth.</p>\n<p>While truculent and violent, twigjacks care deeply for what they consider to be their forests. These creatures harass outsiders who delve deep into their wooded domains, forcing back even the most determined explorers, foresters, and travelers, especially when those intruders cut roads through the forest. However, they are not terribly territorial when it comes to other forest creatures. When sylvan creatures, especially fey, rally against an outside threat, twigjacks in the area eagerly arrive to fight, even if they were not invited.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Bramble Jump","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["plant","primal","teleportation","wood"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the twigjack is in undergrowth, it can instantly teleport to a square of undergrowth within 60 feet. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Splinter Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The twigjack sprays a barrage of splinters and brambles from its body that deals 4d6 piercing damage in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 20 basic Reflex save. The twigjack can't use Splinter Spray again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/umbral-gnome-rockwarden-bb":{"gear":["Sling","Scythe","Hide Armor","Primal Symbol","Sling Bullets (10)"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>A notable subgroup of gnomes called umbral gnomes typically have gray or brown skin with a stony texture, and thin, pale hair or bald pates. Umbral gnomes are most numerous in the Darklands, where they go by the name drathnelar. While they are not as sinister or ruthless as other Darklands denizens, those who seek their aid should remember that they don't welcome strangers with open arms.</p>\n<p>Umbral gnome rockwardens follow druidic teachings and commune with the natural elemental influences and denizens of the Darklands.</p>"},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/umbral-gnome-scout-bb":{"gear":["Sling","Sickle","Sling Bullets (20)"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Umbral gnome scouts patrol the tunnels that lead into their settlements. They make use of the darkness of these tunnels to hide from any would-be trespassers. While umbral gnome scouts prefer to use their stealth for reconnaissance, they aren't afraid to strike from the shadows to deal with threats. They are adept at moving between areas of darkness for hit-and-run tactics.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Hidden Movement","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the umbral gnome scout starts their turn Undetected or Hidden to a creature, that creature is Off-Guard against the umbral gnome scout's attacks until the end of the turn.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/umbral-gnome-warrior-bb":{"gear":["Heavy Crossbow","Spear","Steel Shield","Studded Leather Armor","Bolts (20)"],"notes":{"ac":"(20 with shield raised)"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Umbral gnome warriors are quick to charge into battle, but focus on defending their kin and their homes over more aggressive tactics when a choice is available. These warriors tend to work in groups and use their shields to intercept attacks.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Raise a Shield","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The umbral gnome warrior lifts up their shield to get a +2 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the umbral gnome warrior has their shield raised, they can spend your reaction to block a physical attack. Reduce the amount of damage by 5, but then the umbral gnome warrior and their shield both take any damage leftover. This might break or destroy the shield. The shield has a maximum of 20 Hit Points.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/viper-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Each member of this family of venomous snakes has long, hinged fangs that inject potent venom into their prey. Different vipers inject different types of venom, which might result in paralysis, extreme pain and swelling, blood clotting, or even the sudden stopping of the victim's heart.</p>\n<p>Though far less of an imposing physical threat than a giant viper, a common viper poses far more danger than its size would suggest. A viper mainly hunts small mammals or lizards but will attack a humanoid it perceives as a threat.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Slink","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a creature ends its movement adjacent to the viper or within the viper's space, the viper can use its reaction to Stride, Climb, or Swim up to 10 feet. It must end its movement in a location that isn't within 5 feet of a foe. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Viper Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target damaged by the viper's fangs must succeed at a DC 16 Fortitude save or take 1d10 poison damage.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/warg-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Wargs are often mistaken for wolves, but they have a cunning intelligence and the ability to speak. Wargs often form hunting parties with orcs and hobgoblins. Most wargs are amenable to this arrangement, but if food should run out, wargs are more than willing to integrate goblinoid flesh into their diet.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Avenging Bite","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature within the reach of the warg's bite attacks one of its allies, the warg can spend its reaction to make a jaws Strike against that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Pack Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The warg's jaws Strike deals 1d4 extra damage to creatures within reach of two of the warg's allies.</p>"},{"n":"Shred","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the warg has a creature Grabbed, they can spend one action to shred it with their teeth. The creature takes 1d6 slashing damage and can attempt a DC 18 basic Fortitude save.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the warg succeeds at its jaws Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the warg's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/water-scamp-bb":{"notes":{"hp":"fast healing 2 (while underwater)"},"flavor":"<p>Elemental scamps are bat-like critters marked by elemental powers. Water scamps are marked apart from other scamps by sleek fur that traps a layer of water next to their skin. Although they can fly like their kin and conjure enough water to never dry out, water scamps leave the water only when they must.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Fast Healing 2 (While Underwater)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with this ability regains the given number of Hit Points each round at the beginning of its turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Acid Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["acid","arcane"],"f":"","d":"<p>The water scamp breathes acid that deals 2d6 acid damage in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 17 basic Reflex save. The water scamp can't use Acid Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Drench","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The water scamp shakes out a seemingly endless supply of water from its fur to put out all non-magical fires within 5 feet.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/web-lurker-bb":{"lang":["spider speak"],"flavor":"<p>Web lurkers, known also as ettercaps, are ugly monsters that not only dwell within the lairs of spiders and swarms, but actively cultivate and shepherd such vermin. Web lurkers hunt in forests, swamps, or scrubby hill lands. They construct structures from their webs high up in trees or within craggy, high canyons, and they surround their territory with traps constructed of the same webbing and natural material.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spider Speak","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The web lurker can speak with and understand spiders.</p>"},{"n":"Web Lurker Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A target damaged by the web lurker's fangs must succeed at a DC 19 Fortitude save or take 1d12 poison damage and gain the Off-Guard condition for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Web Trap","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by the web lurker's web attack gets stuck to the nearest surface. It can't move until it successfully Escapes.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/wight-bb":{"gear":["Dagger"],"flavor":"<p>Wights are undead humanoids that lurk in burial grounds, catacombs, or other places of the dead.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Final Spite","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the wight is reduced to 0 Hit Points, they can use their reaction to make a Strike before being destroyed. They don't gain any Hit Points from corrupting spite on this Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Corrupting Spite","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the wight deals damage to a living creature with their claw or dagger Strike, the wight regains 2 healing Hit Points and the target must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or take 2 damage that can't be healed. The wight can use corrupting spite multiple times, but a single creature can't take more than 8 unhealable damage. Each full night of rest heals 2 of the unhealable damage, and a full day of bed rest increases the recovery of the unhealable damage to 4.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/wolf-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Wolves roam forests, hills, and other wild lands where they live and hunt in packs. Contrary to popular belief, these packs aren't led by the strongest in the group, but typically consist of a mated pair, their pups, and juvenile offspring from previous mating seasons. Offspring generally leave their parents' pack upon reaching maturity, at which point they seek out mates of their own to form their own packs elsewhere. Wolves don't typically view humanoids as prey animals, but extraordinary circumstances can lead wolves to attack people, especially in winter months and other situations where traditional prey (such as deer and elk) are scarce.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Pack Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The wolf's jaws Strike deals 1d4 extra damage to creatures within reach of two of the wolf's allies.</p>"},{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the wolf succeeds at its jaws Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Trip the target. This Trip doesn't apply or count toward the wolf's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/xulgath-leader-bb":{"gear":["Greataxe","Javelin (4)","Breastplate"],"flavor":"<p>Xulgath leaders exhibit greater strength and more affinity for violence than other members of a xulgath community.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Stench","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that comes within 30 feet of the xulgath and can smell the xulgath must attempt a DC 19 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature takes a –1 status penalty to all checks and DCs until it uses an action to retch (Sickened 1). A creature that succeeds at its save isn't affected by any xulgaths' stenches for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Swipe","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The xulgath leader makes two Strikes with their greataxe against two adjacent foes, both of whom are within their reach, with a +1 circumstance bonus. The second attack uses the same multiple attack penalty as the first, but attacks the xulgath boss makes after this take a –10 multiple attack penalty (or a –8 multiple attack penalty for its claw).</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/xulgath-warrior-bb":{"gear":["Club","Javelin (3)"],"flavor":"<p>Reptilian humanoids living underground, xulgaths (known as troglodytes to many surface dwellers) attack intruders in their territory on sight. They live in familial communities, battling rival groups and other aggressive underground inhabitants to survive. They occasionally raid surface settlements, usually at the behest of cruel, bloodthirsty leaders. A typical xulgath has dull gray, dark gray, or ashen scales with a long tail and bony protrusions down the length of their spine.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Stench","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that comes within 30 feet of the xulgath and can smell the xulgath must attempt a DC 16 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature takes a –1 status penalty to all checks and DCs until it uses an action to retch (Sickened 1). A creature that succeeds at its save isn't affected by any xulgaths' stenches for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/menace-under-otari/zephyr-hawk-bb":{"flavor":"<p>Air elementals, such as a zephyr hawk, appear in a variety of sizes and shapes. From the Plane of Air, zephyr hawks are often summoned to be used as airborne messengers. Air elementals can also arrive spontaneously during powerful storms and tornadoes where elemental vortexes form.</p>\n<p>Zephyr hawks appear to be made of clouds, with distinct shapes that give them the appearance of having the wings and beaks of birds. When one sees clouds that resemble animals, they're often unknowingly observing air elementals. Zephyr hawks sometimes drift among wind currents in great flocks called casts.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Circling Attack","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The zephyr hawk flies up to half its Speed, makes two wing Strikes, then flies up to half its Speed again to return to its original location. The second half of this movement doesn't trigger reactions like Reactive Strike. The second attack uses the same multiple attack penalty as the first, but attacks it makes after this take a -8 multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"menace-under-otari-bestiary/secrets-of-the-unlit-star/zombie-shambler-bb":{"flavor":"<p>A zombie's only desire is to consume the living. Unthinking and ever-shambling harbingers of death, zombies stop only when they're destroyed. Among the living dead, zombies are most often used as fodder, wearing down defenses before more powerful undead arrive to deal the killing blow. Zombies can't truly think for themselves, but they can be commanded by other allied undead and powerful necromancers.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Slow","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A zombie has only 2 actions on its turn, and it can't use reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the zombie succeeds at its fist Strike, it can use this action immediately after to attempt to Grapple the target. This Grapple doesn't apply or count toward the zombie's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Jaws":"<p>If the zombie has a creature Grabbed or Restrained, it can attempt this special Strike against the grabbed or restrained creature.</p>"}}});
